  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-183533",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is composite,}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
